{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771178802520,"sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","part":{"id":"prt_c6278da0c001sQqv9G1JG0f7YP","sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","messageID":"msg_c6278c39a001nHM4zjM7G8gFKx","type":"tool","callID":"call_8f69e79932c54353a43a3c0b","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"subagent_type":"explore","description":"Study specs/* exhaustively","prompt":"Study all files in specs/ directory. Read each file thoroughly and provide a comprehensive summary of all the application specifications. Include all requirements, features, constraints, and any other important details. Be very thorough."},"output":"task_id: ses_39d8725e2ffeUg1BCvCq8b5ZBy (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n# Comprehensive Application Specifications Summary\n\nBased on thorough analysis of all 12 specification files, here is a complete summary of the Game of Life application:\n\n---\n\n## Core Architecture Overview\n\nThe application is a **strategic, level-based Game of Life** where players must maximize their score within time limits and Flux (resource) constraints. The game features a cinematic presentation, real-time audio feedback, and advanced pattern detection for scoring.\n\n---\n\n## Phase Management System\n\n### Three-Phase State Machine\n\n**1. PLANNING Phase**\n- Duration: Unlimited (player-controlled)\n- Actions: Place/remove cells using Flux resource\n- Entry: Level initialization or restart\n- Exit: Player clicks START button (requires ≥1 cell placed)\n- Features: Full Flux refund on cell removal\n\n**2. RUNNING Phase**\n- Entry: After 3-second countdown (3, 2, 1...)\n- Duration: Fixed timer (starts at 45 seconds, increases by 15s per level)\n- Actions: Add-only cell placement using saved Flux (no removal)\n- Simulation: Conway's Game of Life rules execute automatically\n- Exit Conditions:\n  - Timer reaches 0 → FINISHED\n  - All cells die → FINISHED (immediate level end)\n\n**3. FINISHED Phase**\n- Duration: 2.0s pause before auto-advance\n- Actions: View-only mode\n- Display: Final score, cells alive\n- Exit: Auto-advance to next level with fade transition\n\n**Important Constraints:**\n- No simulation carryover between levels (fresh grid, fresh Flux each level)\n- Timer continues running when browser tab is inactive\n- Phase transitions are guarded (cannot skip phases)\n- COUNTDOWN phase added between PLANNING and RUNNING\n\n---\n\n## Level Progression System\n\n### Difficulty Scaling (Configurable)\n\n**Default Strategy: Increase Time**\n- Level 1: 45 seconds, 20 Flux\n- Level 2: 60 seconds, 20 Flux\n- Level 3: 75 seconds, 20 Flux\n- Level N: `45 + (N-1) * 15` seconds, constant 20 Flux\n\n**Alternative Strategies (Expert Settings):**\n- Time Only: Increase time, constant Flux\n- Resource Only: Constant time, decrease Flux\n- Mixed: Both time and Flux adjusted\n- Extreme: Slight time increase, aggressive Flux reduction\n\n### Game Objectives\n- **Goal**: Maximize points within time limit and Flux budget\n- **No Lose Condition**: Game always advances to next level; only score varies\n- **End Game**: After configurable number of levels (default: 10)\n- **Victory**: Show total accumulated score with \"Play Again\" or \"Return to Menu\"\n\n### Level Progression Flow\n1. Complete level N (timer = 0 OR all cells die)\n2. Fade out (2.0s)\n3. Interstitial black screen with \"Level X Complete\" fading to \"Level X+1\" (2.0s)\n4. Fade in to level N+1 (2.0s)\n5. Reset to PLANNING phase with fresh grid and Flux\n6. Score accumulated across all levels (tracked separately per level)\n\n---\n\n## Flux Resource Management\n\n### Core Mechanics\n- **Initial Allocation**: 20 Flux per level (configurable: 5-50)\n- **Placement Cost**: Exactly 1 Flux per cell (same cost in both phases)\n- **Refund**: Full refund (1 Flux) when removing cells during PLANNING phase only\n- **Play Phase**: No refunds, add-only placement using saved Flux\n- **Strategic Decision**: Players decide how much Flux to use during planning vs save for play\n\n### Validation Rules\n- Cannot place cell if Flux < 1\n- Cannot place outside grid bounds\n- Refund applies ONLY during PLANNING phase\n- No refunds during RUNNING or FINISHED phases\n- Can place cells during RUNNING phase if Flux remains\n\n### UI Requirements\n- Location: Bottom center of screen\n- Visual: Bar or counter showing current/initial\n- Color Coding: Green/Yellow (plenty) → Orange (<30%) → Red (0)\n- Animation: Smooth transitions\n- Feedback: Error sound/red flash on insufficient Flux\n\n---\n\n## Scoring System\n\n### Scoring Formula\n\n```typescript\ngenerationScore = (movers × 10 + oscillators × 2) × multiplier\n```\n\n**Default Parameters:**\n- Movers: 10 points per generation\n- Oscillators: 2 points per generation\n- Static patterns: 0 points\n- Score multiplier: 1.0\n\n**Per-Level Behavior:**\n- Score resets to 0 at each level start (no carryover)\n- Real-time updates every generation during RUNNING phase\n- Smooth number counting animation (lerp over 0.2s)\n- Brief flash every 100 points (optional)\n- Maximum score cap: 9,007,199,254,740,991\n\n**High Score Tracking:**\n- Save highest score per level to localStorage\n- Not used for game completion, only for player progress tracking\n\n### Display\n- Location: Top-left of screen\n- Format: Large number with \"PTS\" label\n- Animation: Smooth increment with pulse/flash on point gain\n- Optional: Pattern breakdown (Active Movers, Oscillators, Rate)\n\n---\n\n## Movement Detection & Pattern Classification\n\n### Classification Algorithm\n\n**Pattern Types:**\n1. **MOVER**: Centroid translates (|dx| > threshold OR |dy| > threshold)\n2. **OSCILLATOR**: Centroid static, cell set changes\n3. **STATIC**: Centroid static, cell set unchanged\n\n**Default Configuration:**\n- Centroid history length: 5 generations\n- Movement threshold: 0.5 cells\n- Minimum cluster size: 1 cell\n\n**Algorithm Steps:**\n1. Identify connected cell clusters (8-connectivity, includes diagonals)\n2. Calculate centroid (average of all cell positions)\n3. Track centroid history across generations\n4. Calculate velocity: `dx = (current.x - history[0].x) / historyLength`\n5. Classify based on movement and cell set changes\n6. Match clusters across generations by nearest centroid\n\n**Edge Cases:**\n- Cluster split: Track both as new clusters\n- Cluster merge: Classification reset to avoid double-counting\n- Glider guns: Stationary structure = Static, produced gliders = Movers\n\n**Performance:**\n- Must process < 16ms for 60fps\n- Scales with game grid sizes (20×30, 40×50, 60×80)\n- Optimization: Recompute centroids only for changed regions\n\n---\n\n## User Interaction System\n\n### Interaction Modes\n- **Draw Mode**: Click/drag to place live cells (age=1)\n- **Erase Mode**: Click/drag to remove cells (set to 0)\n\n### Mouse Interaction\n- Mouse Down: Capture position, convert to grid coordinates, trigger 'down'\n- Mouse Move (while pressed): Capture position, convert to grid, trigger 'enter'\n- Mouse Up (global): Set isMouseDown to false\n- Coordinate mapping: `c = floor(x / (canvasWidth / numCols))`\n\n### Touch Interaction\n- Touch Start/Move: Prevent default (stop scrolling), capture position, convert to grid\n- Touch End/Cancel: Set isMouseDown to false\n- Touch action: `touch-action: none` on canvas\n- Multi-touch: Only first touch used (ignore additional)\n\n### Grid Interaction Constraints\n- Disabled during RUNNING and FINISHED phases\n- START button disabled until ≥1 cell placed\n- Minimum 44×44px touch targets for mobile accessibility\n- Cell coordinates: `cellX = Math.floor((x - gridOffsetX) / cellSize)`\n\n---\n\n## Canvas Rendering System\n\n### Dark Neon Theme\n- Background: `#0a0a0f` (very dark blue-black)\n- Grid lines: `#1a1a2e` (subtle, only during PLANNING phase)\n\n### Age-Based Cell Colors\n- Age 0 (just born): `#00ffff` (bright cyan) - 15px glow\n- Age 1-2: `#61dafb` (React blue) - 8px glow\n- Age 3-5: `#ff00ff` (magenta/pink) - 4px glow\n- Age 6+: `#4a00ff` (deep purple) - 2px glow\n\n### Rendering Pipeline\n1. Canvas resize (update width/height if changed)\n2. Transform reset (clear and apply DPR scaling)\n3. Draw loop: Clear background → Draw grid lines (if enabled) → Draw live cells\n4. Intensity update: Set CSS variable `--life-intensity`\n\n### Responsive Cell Sizing\n- Mobile (<768px): 18px cells\n- Desktop (≥768px): 20px cells\n- Minimum 10 cells visible in smallest dimension\n- Cell size updates on window resize\n\n### Performance Optimizations\n- Use `window.devicePixelRatio` for sharp rendering\n- Minimize context state changes\n- Dependency tracking with useCallback\n- DPR scaling for retina displays\n\n---\n\n## Audio Sonification System\n\n### Sound Engine Interface\n\n```typescript\ninterface SoundEngine {\n  setEnabled(enabled: boolean): void;\n  setVolume(volume: number): void;\n  setWaveform(waveform: OscillatorType): void;\n  playGenerationSound(bornCount: number, avgRow: number, totalRows: number): void;\n  playInteractionSound(type: 'draw' | 'erase'): void;\n}\n```\n\n### Generation Sounds\n- **Trigger**: After each simulation step with bornCount > 0\n- **Pitch Mapping**: Based on average row position of new births\n  - Formula: `pitch = (1 - avgRow / totalRows) × frequencyRange`\n  - Higher rows (top) = higher pitch\n  - Lower rows (bottom) = lower pitch\n- **Intensity**: More births = louder/more prominent sound\n- **Duration**: Short, ~100-200ms\n- **Volume**: baseVolume × bornCount scaling\n\n### Interaction Sounds\n- **Draw**: Higher pitch (~880Hz), short duration (~50ms)\n- **Erase**: Lower pitch (~440Hz), short duration (~50ms)\n- Both use baseVolume setting\n\n### Waveform Types\n- **sine**: Smooth, pure tone (default)\n- **triangle**: Slightly richer harmonics\n- **square**: Harsh, buzzy tone\n- **sawtooth**: Bright, brassy tone\n\n### Volume Control\n- Range: 0.0 to 0.5\n- Default: 0.1 (10%)\n- UI Slider: 10ms steps, displays percentage (volume × 200%)\n\n### Browser Requirements\n- Web Audio API required\n- Modern browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n- iOS: Requires user gesture to start\n- Autoplay policy: Context starts suspended, resumed on first interaction\n- Lazy initialization: Create AudioContext on first sound play\n\n---\n\n## UI/Overlay System\n\n### Cinematic Intro Overlay\n- Shows on app load\n- Title: \"CONWAY'S GAME OF LIFE\" with glitch effect\n- CTA button: \"ENTER VOID\"\n- Exit animation: 1.2s fade/scale transition\n- Game renders in background during intro\n\n### Main Controls (Glass HUD)\n\n**Main Control Buttons:**\n- **PLAY/PAUSE**: Toggle simulation running state\n- **STEP**: Execute single generation (disabled while running)\n- **RANDOM**: Fill grid randomly (15% cell density)\n- **CLEAR**: Remove all cells, reset generation (red text color)\n\n**Interaction Mode Buttons:**\n- **DRAW**: Enable cell placement mode (active state highlighted)\n- **ERASE**: Enable cell removal mode (active state highlighted)\n\n**Status Controls:**\n- **Waveform Selector**: Dropdown (Sine, Triangle, Square, Saw)\n- **Volume Slider**: Range 0-0.5, 0.01 step\n- **Generation Counter**: Display \"GEN: {number}\"\n- **Settings Toggle**: Gear icon button (⚙️)\n\n### Settings Panel\n\n**Configuration Options:**\n1. **Speed**: Slider (10ms to 500ms)\n2. **Grid Size**: Small (20×30), Medium (40×50), Large (60×80)\n3. **Visuals**: Checkbox for grid lines\n4. **Audio**: Checkbox for sonification\n5. **Expert Settings**: Access to Expert Settings panel\n\n### Phase Status Display\n- Always visible\n- Shows current phase: PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED\n- Timer display (COUNTDOWN and RUNNING phases)\n- Flux counter (PLANNING and RUNNING phases)\n\n### Glass Effect CSS\n```css\nbackground: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);\nbackdrop-filter: blur(10px);\nborder: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2);\nborder-radius: 12px;\n```\n\n### Responsive Design\n- Desktop: Full width HUD centered at bottom\n- Mobile: Controls may stack or scroll\n- Touch: Minimum 44px touch targets\n- Canvas: Adapts to window size, grid scales accordingly\n\n---\n\n## Auto-Advance Transitions\n\n### Transition Sequence (Success)\n\n**1. FINISHED Phase Display (2.0s):**\n- Show final score\n- Show \"Level Complete\" text\n- Continue rendering simulation (visual only, no scoring)\n- SKIP: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade out\n\n**2. Fade Out (2.0s):**\n- Full-screen black overlay opacity 0→1\n- Easing: ease-in-out\n- Simulation continues but hidden\n- SKIP: Press Space/ESC to skip to interstitial\n\n**3. Interstitial (2.0s):**\n- Full black screen\n- \"Level X Complete\" (fading out) → \"Level X+1\" (fading in)\n- Load next level configuration\n- Reset game state (Flux, Score resets - no carryover)\n- SKIP: Press Space/ESC to skip to fade in\n\n**4. Fade In (2.0s):**\n- Black overlay opacity 1→0\n- New level visible with fresh grid\n- Simulation stopped, waiting for countdown\n- PLANNING phase ready after countdown\n- SKIP: Press Space/ESC to skip to READY\n\n**5. READY:**\n- Player can immediately start placing cells\n\n### Transition Config\n```typescript\ninterface TransitionConfig {\n  fadeOutDuration: number;        // 2.0s\n  fadeInDuration: number;         // 2.0s\n  interstitialDuration: number;   // 2.0s\n  autoAdvanceDelay: number;       // 2.0s\n  skipEnabled: boolean;           // Allow skipping (Space/ESC)\n}\n```\n\n### Failure Transition\n- Similar fade sequence to \"Game Over\" screen\n- Options: \"Retry Level\" or \"Return to Menu\"\n- No auto-advance on failure (wait for input)\n\n### Final Level\n- After final level: Fade to \"Victory\" screen\n- Show total score accumulated across all levels\n- Options: \"Play Again\" or \"Return to Level 1\"\n\n### Special Cases\n- **Browser Tab During Transition**: Pause transition timer, resume when active\n- **Rapid Success**: Allow holding Space/ESC to skip all transitions\n- **Performance**: Use `will-change: opacity` for smooth 60fps fades\n- **Accessibility**: Reduced motion preferences support\n\n---\n\n## Expert Settings / Dev Panel\n\n### Access Methods\n- Keyboard: '`' (backtick) for quick access\n- Menu: \"Settings → Advanced → Expert Mode\" (if menu exists)\n- Mobile: Triple-tap top-left corner\n\n### Configurable Parameters\n\n**Movement Detection:**\n- Centroid history length: 3-10 (default: 5)\n- Movement threshold: 0.1-2.0 cells (default: 0.5)\n- Minimum cluster size: 1-5 (default: 1)\n\n**Scoring:**\n- Mover points per generation: 1-100 (default: 10)\n- Oscillator points per generation: 0-20 (default: 2)\n- Score multiplier: 0.1-5.0 (default: 1.0)\n\n**Level Generation:**\n- Base time: 10-120 seconds (default: 45)\n- Time increment per level: 0-60 seconds (default: 15)\n- Base Flux: 5-50 (default: 20)\n- Difficulty scaling mode: TIME_ONLY | RESOURCE_ONLY | MIXED | EXTREME\n\n**Grid Sizing:**\n- Mobile cell size: 14-24px (default: 18)\n- Desktop cell size: 16-28px (default: 20)\n- Minimum visible cells: 10\n\n### UI Requirements\n- Modal overlay, centered or right sidebar\n- Collapsible sections by category\n- Sliders for numeric ranges, number inputs for precision\n- Dropdowns for mode selection\n- Changes apply immediately (no restart required)\n- Visual indicator when value differs from default\n- \"Revert\" button per section\n- \"Export JSON\" / \"Import JSON\" for sharing configurations\n- \"Reset to Defaults\" with confirmation\n\n### Persistence\n- Save to localStorage under key `gol-expert-settings`\n- Load on app startup\n- Schema validation (Zod or similar)\n- Corrupted storage: fall back to defaults\n\n### Danger Zone\n- Separate section for \"Break Things\" settings\n- Require confirmation for extreme values\n- Show warning if settings would make game impossible\n\n---\n\n## Core Simulation Engine\n\n### Rule Set (Conway's Standard)\n- **Born**: Exactly 3 neighbors\n- **Survive**: 2 or 3 neighbors\n- **Die**: All other cases\n\n### Grid Computation\n- **Cell State**: Integer (0 = dead, >0 = alive, value = age in generations)\n- **Neighborhood**: Moore neighborhood (8 adjacent cells, includes diagonals)\n- **Boundary Conditions**: Toroidal (wraps edges using modulo arithmetic)\n- **Age Tracking**: Surviving cells increment age each generation\n\n### Simulation Step Process\n1. Create deep copy of current grid (double buffer)\n2. Iterate through all cells\n3. Count neighbors using modulo: `(i + x + rows) % rows`\n4. Apply rule set (born/survive arrays)\n5. Update cell state (0 = death, 1 = birth, age+1 = survival)\n6. Swap buffers\n\n### Performance Optimization\n- Direct grid access using React ref (avoid re-renders)\n- Precomputed neighbor offset array\n- Generation counter triggers render only when needed\n- `requestAnimationFrame` with delta time check\n\n### Data Structures\n```typescript\ntype GridType = number[][];\ninterface SimulationState {\n  grid: GridType;\n  generation: number;\n  running: boolean;\n  speed: number; // ms between steps\n  selectedRule: RuleSet;\n}\n```\n\n### Speed Control\n- Configurable: 10ms to 500ms between steps\n- Speed ref used in animation loop (no state dependency)\n- Updated immediately on change\n\n---\n\n## Key Constraints & Edge Cases\n\n### Browser Compatibility\n- Web Audio API required for sonification\n- Modern browsers: Chrome, Firefox, Safari, Edge\n- iOS: User gesture required to start audio\n- Autoplay policy: AudioContext starts suspended\n\n### Performance Requirements\n- Movement detection: < 16ms for 60fps (scales with grid sizes)\n- Canvas rendering: Optimized with DPR scaling and minimal state changes\n- Score calculation: Decoupled from render if heavy\n\n### Edge Cases by System\n\n**Phase Management:**\n- Zero cells at start: START button disabled\n- All cells die early: Level ends immediately\n- Browser tab switch: Timer continues during gameplay, pauses during transitions\n- Rapid phase switching: Prevent multiple START clicks\n- Countdown: No input allowed\n\n**Flux Management:**\n- Zero Flux at start: Prevent level start\n- Lag between click and update: Atomic Flux decrement with placement\n- Play phase placement: Queue if mid-simulation step\n\n**Movement Detection:**\n- Cluster split/merge: Track new clusters or reset classification\n- Single isolated cell: Treat as cluster size 1\n- Large grids: Scale algorithm to actual game sizes (20×30 to 60×80)\n\n**Canvas Rendering:**\n- Canvas resize: Handle width/height, DPR, cell size together\n- Empty grid: Draw only grid lines (if enabled)\n- High cell count: May have issues with 500+ cells\n\n**Audio Sonification:**\n- No births: Sound not triggered\n- Suspended context: Resume on next interaction\n- Volume = 0: Sounds generated at 0 gain\n- Multiple events: Polyphonic (concurrent sounds allowed)\n\n**Auto-Advance Transitions:**\n- Browser tab switch: Pause transition timer\n- Last level: Victory screen instead of next level\n- Low-end devices: Use `will-change: opacity`, consider reduced animation complexity\n\n---\n\n## Implementation Notes Summary\n\n### Technology Stack\n- React with hooks (useState, useReducer, useCallback, useRef)\n- HTML5 Canvas for rendering\n- Web Audio API for sonification\n- CSS animations and transitions\n- LocalStorage for persistence\n\n### State Management\n- Phase management: React useReducer for state machine\n- Flux: useState or useReducer\n- Expert settings: React Context or Zustand\n- Grid: React ref for direct access (avoid re-renders)\n\n### Performance\n- Direct grid access via ref (simulation)\n- Precomputed neighbor offsets\n- DPR scaling for retina displays\n- Circular buffer for centroid history\n- Optimize canvas draws (minimize state changes)\n- Lazy initialization for AudioContext\n\n### Accessibility\n- Reduced motion preferences support\n- Minimum 44px touch targets\n- Keyboard shortcuts (G for grid lines, Space/ESC for transitions)\n- Audio feedback for interactions\n\n### Testing Considerations\n- Test all browser zoom levels for overlay coverage\n- Test with all transition skip combinations\n- Verify scoring determinism (same patterns = same score)\n- Validate all input ranges and constraints\n- Test tab switching behavior (gameplay vs transitions)\n\n---\n\n## All Default Values Summary\n\n| Parameter | Default | Range |\n|-----------|---------|-------|\n| Initial Flux | 20 | 5-50 |\n| Base Time | 45 seconds | 10-120 seconds |\n| Time Increment | 15 seconds | 0-60 seconds |\n| Mover Points | 10/gen | 1-100 |\n| Oscillator Points | 2/gen | 0-20 |\n| Score Multiplier | 1.0 | 0.1-5.0 |\n| Centroid History | 5 generations | 3-10 |\n| Movement Threshold | 0.5 cells | 0.1-2.0 |\n| Simulation Speed | 100ms | 10-500ms |\n| Audio Volume | 0.1 | 0.0-0.5 |\n| Mobile Cell Size | 18px | 14-24px |\n| Desktop Cell Size | 20px | 16-28px |\n\n---\n\nThis comprehensive specification defines a sophisticated, level-based Game of Life game that combines classic cellular automaton mechanics with modern game design elements including resource management, real-time scoring, cinematic presentation, and audio feedback.\n</task_result>","title":"Study specs/* exhaustively","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d8725e2ffeUg1BCvCq8b5ZBy","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771178613273,"end":1771178802517}}}}
