  color: #ffaa00;\n}\n\n.hud-status-value.red {\n  color: #ff4444;\n}\n```\n\n### Color Scheme Summary:\n\nThe implementation uses **three colors** based on the flux ratio:\n- **Red**: `#ff4444` - when flux ratio ≤ 0 or flux ≤ 5 (in Game.tsx)\n- **Orange**: `#ffaa00` - when flux ratio < 0.5 or flux between 5-10 (in Game.tsx)\n- **Green**: `#00ff00` - when flux ratio ≥ 0.5 or flux > 10 (in Game.tsx)\n\n**Note**: The implementation currently does not include a \"yellow\" color, only green, orange, and red.\n\n### Related Type Definition: `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts`\n\n**FluxState Interface (lines 36-41):**\n```typescript\nexport interface FluxState {\n  current: number\n  initial: number\n  placed: number\n  removed: number\n}\n```\n</task_result>","title":"Find Flux counter display","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d840db9ffeHn0YZV06WhlVuK","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771178816067,"end":1771178934031}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771178939287,"sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","part":{"id":"prt_c627bf218001rx2TTbNrRGbDaF","sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","messageID":"msg_c627bbe37001ESPebeaUX6rVUI","type":"tool","callID":"call_fc1a90f80c714a3f882d0d8f","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find phase status display","prompt":"Search for phase status indicator component in the codebase. Look for components that show current phase (PLANNING, COUNTDOWN, RUNNING, FINISHED). Search for \"phase\", \"status\" in src/components/.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d840dd4ffebPD9TiPMjvryEd (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Search Results: Phase Status Indicator Component\n\nI found the phase status indicator components in the codebase. Here's a comprehensive overview:\n\n### Primary Component: **GlassHUD** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`)\n\nThis is the main component that displays the current phase status. Key features:\n\n**Location:** Lines 126-129 in GlassHUD.tsx\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"hud-status\">\n  <div className=\"hud-status-item\">\n    <span className=\"hud-status-label\">Phase:</span>\n    <span className=\"hud-status-value\">{phase}</span>\n  </div>\n  <div className=\"hud-status-item\">\n    <span className=\"hud-status-label\">Cells:</span>\n    <span className=\"hud-status-value\">{aliveCount}</span>\n  </div>\n  <div className=\"hud-status-item\">\n    <span className=\"hud-status-label\">Flux:</span>\n    <span className={`hud-status-value ${fluxColor}`}>{flux}</span>\n  </div>\n</div>\n```\n\n### Phase States\nThe component supports four game phases (defined in `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts`):\n- `PLANNING` - Initial setup phase where users can place cells\n- `COUNTDOWN` - 3-second countdown before running\n- `RUNNING` - Active simulation phase with timer\n- `FINISHED` - Completed phase\n\n### Additional Phase Display in Game Component\nThe Game component (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`, lines 173-175) also displays phase-related information:\n\n```tsx\n<div>Phase: {phaseState.current}</div>\n{phaseState.current === 'COUNTDOWN' && <div>Countdown: {phaseState.countdownValue}</div>}\n{phaseState.current === 'RUNNING' && <div>Timer: {phaseState.timerRemaining}s</div>}\n```\n\n### Styling (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/GlassHUD.css`)\n\n**Phase Status Section (lines 145-180):**\n- `.hud-status` - Container for status display with dark background\n- `.hud-status-item` - Individual status item with label and value\n- `.hud-status-label` - Gray/transparent white label text\n- `.hud-status-value` - Cyan colored value text\n- Color variants for flux values: `.green`, `.orange`, `.red`\n\n### Supporting Files\n\n1. **Phase Logic** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/lib/phase.ts`):\n   - Phase state management\n   - Transition rules between phases\n   - Countdown and timer handling\n\n2. **Phase Hook** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/hooks/usePhaseTimer.ts`):\n   - Custom hook for phase timer management\n\n3. **Tests** (`/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.test.tsx`):\n   - Line 39-48: Tests for status display rendering\n   - Line 187-191: Tests for phase text display (START vs RUNNING)\n\n### Key Features\n- Displays current phase prominently\n- Shows phase-specific information (countdown during COUNTDOWN, timer during RUNNING)\n- Flux indicator with color coding based on value\n- Glass-morphism design with backdrop blur effects\n- Responsive layout for mobile devices\n</task_result>","title":"Find phase status display","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d840dd4ffebPD9TiPMjvryEd","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771178816039,"end":1771178939285}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1771178944395,"sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","part":{"id":"prt_c627bf1fa001cnfi8ClaGXUAoR","sessionID":"ses_39d873d0fffe1FxcQovLtdjhwD","messageID":"msg_c627bbe37001ESPebeaUX6rVUI","type":"tool","callID":"call_44f3f3551c6a4502b6a9577a","tool":"task","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"description":"Find interaction mode buttons","prompt":"Search for DRAW and ERASE button implementations in the codebase. Look for components that handle interaction mode toggling. Search in src/components/ for any buttons related to draw/erase modes.","subagent_type":"explore"},"output":"task_id: ses_39d840dfcffe2mLQTud32shinu (for resuming to continue this task if needed)\n\n<task_result>\n## Summary: DRAW and ERASE Button Implementations\n\nI found comprehensive implementations of DRAW and ERASE button functionality throughout the codebase. Here's a detailed breakdown:\n\n### **Type Definition**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/types/index.ts`\n- **Line 5:** Defines the `InteractionMode` type: `'DRAW' | 'ERASE'`\n\n---\n\n### **Main UI Implementation (GlassHUD Component)**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.tsx`\n\n**Lines 76-91:** The DRAW and ERASE buttons in the modern glass-morphism HUD\n\n```tsx\n<div className=\"hud-group\">\n  <button\n    className={`hud-button ${interactionMode === 'DRAW' ? 'active' : ''}`}\n    onClick={() => onSetMode('DRAW')}\n    disabled={!canInteract}\n  >\n    DRAW\n  </button>\n  <button\n    className={`hud-button ${interactionMode === 'ERASE' ? 'active' : ''}`}\n    onClick={() => onSetMode('ERASE')}\n    disabled={!canInteract}\n  >\n    ERASE\n  </button>\n</div>\n```\n\n**Key Features:**\n- Conditional `active` class for visual feedback\n- Disabled state when interaction is not allowed\n- Uses `onSetMode` callback prop to update state\n- Part of a button group layout\n\n---\n\n### **State Management (Game Component)**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/Game.tsx`\n\n**Line 14:** Interaction mode state initialization:\n```tsx\nconst [interactionMode, setInteractionMode] = useState<InteractionMode>('DRAW')\n```\n\n**Lines 145-158:** Legacy standalone button implementation:\n```tsx\n<button\n  onClick={() => setInteractionMode('DRAW')}\n  disabled={phaseState.current !== 'PLANNING'}\n  style={{ backgroundColor: interactionMode === 'DRAW' ? '#61dafb' : '#1a1a1a' }}\n>\n  Draw\n</button>\n<button\n  onClick={() => setInteractionMode('ERASE')}\n  disabled={phaseState.current !== 'PLANNING'}\n  style={{ backgroundColor: interactionMode === 'ERASE' ? '#61dafb' : '#1a1a1a' }}\n>\n  Erase\n</button>\n```\n\n**Note:** This appears to be a duplicate/legacy implementation with inline styles.\n\n---\n\n### **Interaction Logic (GridInteraction Component)**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GridInteraction.tsx`\n\n**Line 16:** Component receives `interactionMode` prop:\n```tsx\ninteractionMode: 'DRAW' | 'ERASE'\n```\n\n**Lines 40-68:** Core interaction logic:\n\n**DRAW Mode (Lines 40-59):**\n- If cell exists: Remove it (in PLANNING phase)\n- If cell doesn't exist: Place it (if flux allows)\n\n**ERASE Mode (Lines 60-69):**\n- Only removes existing cells\n- Only works in PLANNING phase\n\n---\n\n### **Styling (GlassHUD.css)**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/styles/GlassHUD.css`\n\n**Lines 59-63:** Active button styling:\n```css\n.hud-button.active {\n  background: rgba(97, 218, 251, 0.3);\n  border-color: #61dafb;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 15px rgba(97, 218, 251, 0.4);\n}\n```\n\n**Lines 47-51:** Hover effects:\n```css\n.hud-button:hover:not(:disabled) {\n  background: rgba(97, 218, 251, 0.2);\n  border-color: #61dafb;\n  box-shadow: 0 0 10px rgba(97, 218, 251, 0.3);\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n### **Test Coverage**\n**File:** `/home/ochanomizu/repos/game_of_life/src/components/GlassHUD.test.tsx`\n\nMultiple tests verify:\n- Button rendering (lines 32-33)\n- Mode switching functionality (lines 84-88)\n- Button state changes (lines 128-129, 160-164)\n\n---\n\n### **Component Flow**\n```\nGlassHUD (UI)\n    ↓ onSetMode callback\nGame (State Management)\n    ↓ interactionMode prop\nGridInteraction (Logic)\n```\n\nThe implementation provides a clean separation of concerns with proper state management, visual feedback, and comprehensive interaction logic for both draw and erase modes.\n</task_result>","title":"Find interaction mode buttons","metadata":{"sessionId":"ses_39d840dfcffe2mLQTud32shinu","model":{"modelID":"glm-4.7","providerID":"zai-coding-plan"},"truncated":false},"time":{"start":1771178816000,"end":1771178944393}}}}
